{"records":[{"id":"y8dndzn3mg","title":"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication","description":"These data are part of the Supplemental Items associated with the manuscript entitled \"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication\". These files include Supplementary Data file 1-4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-16T10:34:13.579Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y8dndzn3mg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y8dndzn3mg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Limeng","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Screening","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"4mb5kjywkj","title":"Western Blot raw data of the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\"","description":"The raw images of WB is for the reviewers' request when reviewing the manuscript titled \"In vivo CRISPR knockout screen identifies p47 as a suppressor for HER2+ breast cancer metastasis by regulating NEMO trafficking and autophagy flux\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-12-04T00:26:32.621Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/4mb5kjywkj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/4mb5kjywkj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mingang","last_name":"Hao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xn262bshj2","title":"Integrated transcriptional network analysis identifies POU2F2 as a key regulatory transcription factor in atherosclerosis","description":"Replication Data for: Integrated transcriptional network analysis identifies POU2F2 as a key regulatory transcription factor in atherosclerosis","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-02-10T11:04:49.261Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xn262bshj2","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xn262bshj2"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"shengqiong","last_name":"deng","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Data Analysis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"b99vdf3fk6","title":"Reversible disruption of specific transcription factor-DNA interactions using CRISPR/Cas9","description":"Raw images of protein analysis for the manuscript by Shariati et al: Reversible disruption of specific transcription factor-DNA interactions using CRISPR/Cas9","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-03-08T00:57:33.668Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/b99vdf3fk6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/b99vdf3fk6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ali","last_name":"Shariati","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8tzv35n2bs","title":"LINF_320013600","description":"Repressor of differentiation kinase 1 | RDK1\nLeishmania infantum (strain JPCM5)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-09-02T20:48:25.404Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8tzv35n2bs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8tzv35n2bs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"rp8kmnt9v8","title":"Single-cell transcriptomic analysis of honeybee brains identifies vitellogenin as a caste differentiation factor","description":"A phenotype analysis for vitellogenin knock down at honey bee larval stage.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-10-04T13:02:49.954Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/rp8kmnt9v8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/rp8kmnt9v8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Liangliang","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Statistics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xrd623n43s","title":"Single-cell transcriptomic analysis of honeybee brains identifies vitellogenin as caste differentiation-related factor","description":"Raw micrograph data.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-06-06T16:16:49.864Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xrd623n43s","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xrd623n43s"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Liangliang","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Micrography"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3fywkn9scp","title":"RANK ligand converts the NCoR/HDAC3 co-repressor to a PGC1β- and RNA-dependent co-activator of osteoclast gene expression","description":"The nuclear receptor co-repressor (NCoR) complex mediates transcriptional repression dependent on histone deacetylation by histone deacetylase 3 (HDAC3) as a component of the complex.  Unexpectedly, we found that signaling by receptor activator of nuclear factor kappa-Β (RANK) converts the NCoR/HDAC3 co-repressor complex to a co-activator of AP-1 and NFkB target genes that are required for mouse osteoclast differentiation.  Accordingly, the dominant function of NCoR/HDAC3 complexes in response to RANK signaling is to activate, rather than repress, gene expression.  Mechanistically, RANK signaling promotes RNA-dependent interaction of the transcriptional co-activator PGC1b with the NCoR/HDAC3 complex, resulting in activation of PGC1b and inhibition of HDAC3 activity for acetylated histone H3.  Non-coding RNAs Dancr and Rnu12 that are associated with altered human bone homeostasis promote NCoR/HDAC3 complex assembly and are necessary for RANKL-induced osteoclast differentiation in vitro.  These findings may be prototypic for signal-dependent functions of NCoR in other biological contexts. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-09-13T20:18:36.542Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3fywkn9scp","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3fywkn9scp"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yohei","last_name":"Abe","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot","Staining Technique","Computed Tomography"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ztg7pxr6ch","title":"STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency","description":"This dataset contains the original raw and analyzed data supporting the manuscript “STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency”. The study identifies STT3A as an essential regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway and a potential therapeutic target for RNF43-deficient cancers. Included data were generated from key experiments, including Wnt reporter assays (DDT), Western blotting (WB), and CRISPR screen, and other experiments central to the study","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-13T11:26:58.874Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ztg7pxr6ch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ztg7pxr6ch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhengjin","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xyv5tj2rcs","title":"EIF3D orchestrates the homeostasis of multiple signaling pathways governing the primed pluripotent stem cell identity","description":"Pluripotent stem cell identities such as differentiation and infinite proliferation have long been decoded in the frameworks of transcription factor networks, epigenomes, and signal transduction, yet unclear and fragmented. However, directing attention toward translation regulation, the bridge between these events promises to provide new insights into previously unexplained mechanisms. Functional CRISPR interference screening led to the discovery that EIF3D maintains primed pluripotency via selective translation regulation. The loss of EIF3D unbalanced the pluripotency-associated signaling pathways, disrupting primed pluripotency. Furthermore, we found that EIF3D safeguards robust proliferation by managing the translation of multiple p53 regulators that maintain low p53 activity in the undifferentiated state. Therefore, this study provides a paradigm for selective translation regulation that defines the primed pluripotent stem cell identity.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-11-30T14:04:26.679Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xyv5tj2rcs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xyv5tj2rcs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kazutoshi","last_name":"Takahashi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Numerical Analysis","Stem Cell","Flow Cytometry","Photograph"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":123776,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":104,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":123776,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":123311,"restricted":60,"embargoed":405},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2096},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1472},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":567},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":441},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":427},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pes